There are two bugs:
1. When the comment is empty, an empty line gets appended — need to skip the empty comment.
2. The "to catch" loop is off: for verse v, the chain should start from animal v-1 (the one before the current animal) and go down to 0. In the case of verse 2 (spider, index 1), the chain should be "She swallowed the spider to catch the fly." — that is, the chain lines refer to the current animal and everything before it. My loop starts from i = v-2, but it should start from i = v-1.

Also, the horse verse (v=8) should not have any chain lines at all.

Rewrite Verse correctly:

```go
func Verse(v int) string {
	var lines []string
	lines = append(lines, fmt.Sprintf("I know an old lady who swallowed a %s.", animals[v-1].name))
	if c := animals[v-1].comment; c != "" {
		lines = append(lines, c)
	}
	for i := v - 1; i >= 0; i-- {
		if i == 0 {
			lines = append(lines, fmt.Sprintf("She swallowed the %s to catch the fly.", animals[i].name))
		} else {
			lines = append(lines, fmt.Sprintf("She swallowed the %s to catch the %s that wriggled and jiggled and tickled inside her.", animals[i].name, animals[i-1].name))
		}
	}
	if v < len(animals) {
		lines = append(lines, "I don't know why she swallowed the fly. Perhaps she'll die.")
	}
	...
}
```

Wait — for verse 1 (fly, v=1), the chain loop runs from i=0 down to 0, and "She swallowed the fly to catch the fly." gets generated — but the expected verse 1 doesn't have that line. Hmm. Expected verse 1:
```
I know an old lady who swallowed a fly.
I don't know why she swallowed the fly. Perhaps she'll die.
```
So the chain should only run when v > 1: for i := v-1; i >= 0; i-- — for v=1, i starts at 0 and generates the fly line. Therefore the loop should be `for i := v - 1; i > 0; i--` — no wait, for verse 2 (spider, index 1), the chain is "She swallowed the spider to catch the fly." — i=1 (spider) catches the fly. So the loop is i from v-1 down to 1, and when i==1, "to catch the fly". Actually, more simply: loop i from v-1 down to 1, and if i==1 output "to catch the fly", otherwise output "to catch the %s that wriggled...". For v=1, no loop iterations.

Two bugs: the empty comment line is being output, and the chain loop is off by one (also, the horse verse needs to have no chain lines). Rewriting `Verse`:

